# Tests for crossing the bed centre on an arm that can travel through it
# (arm_crosses_centre).  A move that carries straight on through the
# middle takes the other solution of every x/y position - the arm at a
# negative radius, the bed turned the other half turn - so it keeps its
# path and its speed and the bed never turns.  The moves that cross the
# centre in polar_singularity.test by stopping on it and turning the bed
# are the ones this runs straight through, printing included.
#
# test/multi_axis/test_centre_path.py checks the plans, and
# test_kin_6axis.c runs the same crossings through the real step
# compressor on the bed and both gantry motors.  This runs them end to
# end through klippy, which is the one place the toolhead hands the
# branch to the motion queue, and the one place a move onto the centre
# is held back for the move after it.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
CONFIG polar_singularity_cross.cfg

# Home.  Homing R puts the arm on the usual branch, at a positive radius.
G28 X
G28 B
G28 Z
G90
G1 X80 Y0 Z10 F6000

# Straight across the centre: stopped a tenth of a micron short of it,
# then carried on through onto the far side, where the arm radius is
# negative and the bed has not moved
G1 X-80 Y0 F6000

# Round the far side on the negative branch, and back across
G1 X0 Y-80 F6000
G1 X80 Y0 F6000
G1 X-80 Y0 F6000
G1 X-40 Y-40 F6000
G1 X40 Y40 F6000

# A near miss, too close to slow down for, is routed through the centre
# and turns the bed by the few hundredths of a degree it misses by
G1 X-40 Y0.005 F6000
G1 X40 Y0.005 F6000

# Printing straight across, both ways
G1 X40 Y0 Z0.3 F3000
G1 X-40 Y0 E5 F1500
G1 X40 Y0 E10 F1500

# Onto the centre, up and down the axis, and off it at right angles -
# the bed turns a quarter turn at most, whichever side it leaves on
G1 X0 Y0 Z10 F3000
G1 Z30 F600
G1 Z10 F600
G1 X0 Y40 F3000
G1 X0 Y0 F3000
G1 X-40 Y0 F3000
G1 X0 Y0 F3000
G1 X0 Y-40 F3000

# Printing through the centre round a corner: the move onto the centre is
# held back until the next one arrives, and the bed turns on the way
# through while the tool keeps moving and extruding - 30 degrees, then
# 80, then back out 20 degrees off the way in
G1 X40 Y0 Z0.3 F3000
G1 X0 Y0 E12 F1500
G1 X-34.64 Y20 E14 F1500
G1 X0 Y0 E16 F1500
G1 X-13.68 Y-37.59 E18 F1500
G1 X0 Y0 E20 F1500
G1 X0 Y-20 E22 F1500

# Held moves are given up before anything else touches the toolhead: a
# wait, a dwell, reading the position - and then the way out blends alone
G1 X0 Y0 E24 F1500
M400
G1 X30 Y30 E26 F1500
G1 X0 Y0 E28 F1500
G4 P10
G1 X0 Y30 E30 F1500
G1 X0 Y0 E32 F1500
GET_POSITION
G1 X30 Y-30 E34 F1500

# A near miss while printing, close enough to go through the centre
# instead of crawling past it
G1 X-40 Y0.02 E36 F1500
G1 X40 Y0.02 E40 F1500
G1 Z10 F600

# Homing R again from the far side puts the arm back on the usual branch
G1 X-60 Y0 F3000
G28 X
G1 X50 Y0 F3000

GET_POSITION
M84
